    {
      "tension": "Skeptic's own alternative (compulsory insurance, joint enterprise liability) carries an insurability vulnerability for unbounded tail risks — which the NAIICP's pooled fund partially answers",
      "opportunity": "Pre-empt by acknowledging the vulnerability and proposing the excise-tax fund as a reinsurance backstop layered on top of retained liability (Price-Anderson structure), not as a substitute for it. This shows the skeptic has absorbed the strongest counterargument and still rejects immunity as the price."
    }
  ]
